3.2 Baselines
We benchmark our TransWebLLM, trained with TransWebEdu, in a 5-shot setting, against diverse open-source multilingual and monolingual LLMs with comparable parameter sizes, different multilingual pretraining mixtures and data sources.
Our multilingual LLM baselines include: mGPT (1.3B) (Shliazhko et al., 2022), BLOOM (1.1B) (Workshop et al., 2022), Llama3.2 (1.3B) (Dubey et al., 2024), Qwen2 (1.5B) (Yang et al., 2024), Qwen2.5 (1.5B) (Yang et al., 2025), and Gemma (2.6B) (Team et al., 2024). Additionally, we compare against language-specific LLM baselines: Afriteva_v2_large (1B) (Oladipo et al., 2023) for Swahili, BritLLM (3B)8 for Welsh, CroissantLLM (1.3B) (Faysse et al., 2024) for French, EuroLLM (1.7B) (Martins et al., 2024) for Arabic, French, German, Italian, Russian, and Spanish, Jais-family-1p3b (1.3B) (Sengupta et al., 2023) for Arabic, Sailor (1.8B) (Dou et al., 2024a) and Sailor2 (1B) (Dou et al., 2024b) for Indonesian. Furthermore, we include two English-centric baselines in our evaluation: TinyLlama (1.1B) (Zhang et al., 2024), Pythia (1.4B) (Biderman et al., 2023). An overview of baseline models and our TransWebLLM has been shown in Table 11 in Appendix E.
